# The coordinator waits a thousand times its Down bound before it re-places
# a down machine's roles: in practice it never re-places them. The heal
# predicate judges every seed from the audit's configuration in force. The
# gone-machine scenario holds its machine down for good on a coin, so only
# a re-placement heals its journals. The scenario strikes about once in
# 300 seeds, so the fixed seeds of the hunt may hold no strike.
expect: caught
cause: heal: a control journal gets every member a live machine can take within the bound
cause: heal: a matchmaker set gets every member a live machine can take within the bound
cause: heal: a journal gets every member a live machine can take within the bound
cause: sets: a set with a machine to go to leaves a wiped one after chaos
file: crates/lib/paros-coordinator/src/cell/watch.rs
--- find
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after {
--- replace
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after * 1000 {
--- end
